A37 — clear flat textures instead of staging them through the upload buffer

vulkan_create_flat_texture filled the whole image through the device's upload
buffer, which is a fixed 1920x1080x4 bytes. Since A33 the session blank is
created at the full output size, so any output wider than 1080p (2400x1080
phones, 1440p handhelds) hit the size assert in uploadBufferData and gamescope
aborted before its first frame. A flat texture needs no staging at all: it is
a transfer destination already, so one vkCmdClearColorImage fills it. The
upload buffer keeps its size; nothing else uploads an output-sized image.

